^SAMPLE = GSM6675036
!Sample_title = MEF cells, non targeting shRNAcontrol, uninduced control, biol rep3 [NC-3]
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM6675036
!Sample_status = Public on Oct 28 2022
!Sample_submission_date = Oct 25 2022
!Sample_last_update_date = Oct 28 2022
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = Mouse embryonic fibroblasts
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Mus musculus
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 10090
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: Mouse embryonic fibroblasts
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: WT
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: ethanol (same volume with DOX)
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = time point: Day 9
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Cells were lysed in 500 μL TRIzol reagent and incubated at room temperature for 5 minutes. 100 μL chloroform was added and fully mixed. Samples were centrifuged at 14,400 rpm for 15 minutes at 4°C and 250 μL aqueous phase containing RNA was transferred to a new tube. 250 μL isopropanol was added to the aqueous phase and mixed well to precipitate RNA. After incubation 10 min at room temperature, RNA pellet was collected through centrifuging at 14,400 rpm for 15 minutes at 4°C and washed with 500 μL 75% ethanol. The RNA pellet was air-dried for 10 min and resuspended in nuclease-free H2O. Mouse tissue samples were first weighted and homogenized as described above with 1ml TRIzol reagent per 100 mg. After homogenization, chloroform was added and the following steps are same with cell samples. A total amount of 2 µg RNA per sample was used as input material for the RNA sample preparations.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Sequencing libraries were generated using VAHTS mRNA-seq v2 Library Prep Kit for Illumina following manufacturer’s recommendations and index codes were added to attribute sequences to each sample. mRNA was purified from total RNA using poly-T oligo-attached magnetic beads. Fragmentation was carried out using fragmentation buffer. First strand cDNA was synthesized and second strand cDNA synthesis was subsequently performed. Remaining overhangs were converted into blunt ends. After adenylation of 3’ ends of DNA fragments, adaptor with hairpin loop structure were ligated. Then the PCR was performed. At last, Qubit HS quantification, Agilent 2100 Bioanalyzer/Fragment Analyzer 5300 quality control, the final library size of about 350bp. The libraries were sequenced on an Illumina NovaSeq platform to generate 150 bp paired-end reads, according to the manufacturer’s instructions.
!Sample_data_processing = All sequencing raw reads were trimmed using Trim Galore v0.6.6 (https://www.bioinformatics.babraham.ac.uk/projects/trim_galore/) with default settings.
!Sample_data_processing = Trimmed reads were aligned to the Mus musculus reference genome (Mm10) using STAR v2.7.7a (Dobin et al., 2013) in paired-end mode with default parameters.
!Sample_data_processing = Gene level counts were generated using FeatureCounts from Subread v1.6.
!Sample_data_processing = Generated matrix file from read quantification was then used for differential expression (DE) analysis. DE analysis was performed using Bioconductor package DESeq2 with contrast of control and treat groups (as indicated).
!Sample_data_processing = Genes having corrected Padj <0.05 (FDR) and absolute log-fold change greater than 1 were considered to be significantly differentially expressed (DE).
!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: Mm10
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: ProcessedDataMatrix.txt, this file include RPKM values for each sample
!Sample_platform_id = GPL24247
!Sample_contact_name = Baiyu,,He
!Sample_contact_email = hebaiyu@nibs.ac.cn
!Sample_contact_phone = +8613810030825
